  "common_gotchas": [
    "When animating Level TOP parameters, the CPU lookup table is rebuilt whenever a parameter changes, which can reduce performance in otherwise simple feedback loops.",
    "Clamp Input should usually stay Auto, but choose Unclamped for higher bit-depth floating pixel formats when values outside 0-1 must survive.",
    "Use opacity as the clean feedback decay control; brightness and clamp changes can make a valid feedback chain look clipped, black, or washed out.",
    "Luma Level TOP preserves hue and saturation more accurately, but it is slower than Level TOP.",
    "Use Info CHOP gpu_memory_used and pixel format checks when level operations are part of high-resolution or 3D texture feedback chains."
  ],
